    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: I cannot decide this dispute on the record before me, so I am sending it to a human reviewer. The contested SGD 6.00 is held — it is neither refunded to the rider nor released to the driver — until that review is done. This is not a finding for either side.\n\nWhy. The only artifact that measures the route, the driver-app GPS trace EV-GPS-04003, is impaired. The admissibility pre-pass tagged it GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW at weight_multiplier 0.6 because it contains a 450-second stretch with no fixes at all, from 14:11:30 to 14:19:00, whose two bounding fixes are 8,489.6 m apart. That is both more than 90 seconds between consecutive fixes and more than a 500 m straight-line step, so the trace is impaired for policy purposes too (POL-RD-07(a) and (b)), not merely at the schema level.\n\nUnder POL-RD-07(ii) a deviation may not be established on an impaired trace alone; it must be corroborated by an independent source, and there is none in this bundle. The chat log EV-CHAT-04003 carries only 'reached already, downstairs at the drop off' and 'ok 1 min', both about the pickup, and neither message has a waypoint_hint; the counterparty statement is null; the fare breakdown EV-FARE-04003 charges no ERP gantries at all; and the trip record's actual_distance_km of 17.60 km is, by the platform's own note on EV-TRIP-04003, the trace figure rounded to one decimal place — the same measurement, which POL-RD-07(ii) expressly excludes as not independent. The claim is therefore not sustained on the present record, and POL-RD-07(iii) with POL-RD-10(3) requires ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because the missing stretch is a data failure and not a finding for the driver.\n\nThe same conclusion follows from confidence alone. The fact that decides whether this trip deviated — the excess of 4.10 km, or 30.37%, measured from the trace figure of 17.60 km against the booked optimal of 13.50 km — is carried only by the 0.6-weight trace. Under POL-GEN-02(2) my confidence cannot exceed 0.6, and since the platform-wide floor is 0.70, POL-RD-10(1) independently mandates escalation. Confidence is set at 0.6.\n\nWhat the money would have been, and what would decide it. Had the route been carried by an unimpaired trace or an independent source, the arithmetic would be: charged_total 25.08; recomputed_fare ((3.80 + 0.75 x 13.50 + 0.28 x 20) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = 20.325; refund 25.08 - 20.325 = 4.755, rounded up to 4.80. That is 18.96% of the charged total — above the 0.50 de-minimis floor and far below the 90% that would make a full refund — so the rider's round figure of 6.00 is not the sum the policy produces in any event. What the reviewer needs is a record covering the missing 14:11:30-14:19:00 stretch: a GPS export that keeps the track through it, an ERP gantry record placing the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route never uses, a driver or counterparty statement admitting the route, or a platform-derived actual-distance figure computed independently of this trace.\n\nTwo further points. No traffic advisory covering this trip is on file — EV-ADVIS-04003-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 — so no closure-based exoneration under POL-RD-03 is available to the driver, and the absence carries nothing for the rider either. And no referral fires: there is no repeat-deviation pattern to refer (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over completed_trips_90d of 245, and the excess is not a material deviation), and the fare reconciles to the cent with no unmatched charge line, so no billing-integrity referral arises."
