    "confidence": 0.6,
    "explanation": "This ruling is an ESCALATE. No money moves today: the disputed SGD 6.00 is held rather than collected from the rider or released to the driver, until a human reviewer decides the case. Both parties largely agree on the facts, so I will set them out plainly.\n\nThe only artifact that measures this trip's route is the GPS trace EV-GPS-04003, and it is impaired. I say that out loud: the admissibility pre-pass applied issue code GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and gave it weight 0.6, because there is a single 450-second interval with no fixes at all, from 14:11:30 to 14:19:00, and its two bounding fixes lie 8,489.6 m apart in a straight line. Under POL-RD-07 that gap also impairs the trace for policy purposes: 450 s exceeds the 90-second limit (limb a) and the 8,489.6 m step exceeds the 500 m limit (limb b). The trace reads 17.60 km against the booked optimal of 13.50 km on the trip record, an excess of 4.10 km, or 30.37% of optimal. That passes both POL-RD-01 establishment gates (0.8 km and 20%), and I accept the rider's point that 4.10 km is the reading most favourable to the driver, since the straight line drawn across the gap understates rather than overstates the distance actually driven.\n\nThe excess nevertheless cannot be established on this trace alone. POL-RD-07(ii) requires an independent corroborating source and this bundle has none: the chat log EV-CHAT-04003 contains only two pickup messages ('downstairs at the drop off', 'ok 1 min'), with waypoint_hint null on both, so there is no driver admission on the route; the fare breakdown EV-FARE-04003 carries no ERP gantry at all; counterparty_statement is null; and trip_record.actual_distance_km of 17.60 km is, by the platform's own note, the trace figure rounded to one decimal place — the same measurement, which POL-RD-07(ii) expressly excludes as not independent. POL-RD-07(iii) therefore applies: the claim is not sustained on the present record, and the outcome is ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because the missing stretch is a data failure, not a finding for the driver. POL-RD-10(3) makes that escalation mandatory.\n\nIndependently, my confidence is capped below the floor. Under POL-GEN-02(2) my confidence cannot exceed the weight of the artifact carrying the deciding fact. Whether this trip deviated is carried by EV-GPS-04003 alone at weight 0.6; the trip record's distance is that same measurement, not a second independent carrier, so the cap does not move up. A cap of 0.6 sits below the platform-wide floor of 0.70, which is an escalation trigger on its own under POL-RD-10(1). bundle_integrity is context only and does not raise the cap.\n\nWhat would have been awarded on the merits had the trace been unimpaired. You (rider) asked for SGD 6.00, reading 'about 19' against the charged 25.08. The policy arithmetic under POL-RD-02 is: charged_total 25.08; recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 13.5 + 0.28 x 20) x 1.0 surge, the multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier where POL-RD-02 places it, + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP = 20.325; refund = 25.08 - 20.325 = 4.755, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 = SGD 4.80. That is above the 0.50 de minimis and 18.96% of the charge, far below the 90% that would convert it into a FULL_REFUND, so the rider's entitlement on the merits would be a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 4.80, not the SGD 6.00 requested. This figure does not issue today, because the escalation replaces the money outcome.\n\nThe driver's remaining points are accepted. This is not a MATERIAL deviation: 4.10 km and 30.37% fall below the 8.0 km and 50% materiality gates, so POL-RD-06's pattern check is not required, and in any event driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 245 — no pattern, no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral, and no refund uplift. There is also no pass-through or billing-integrity correction to add: the fare breakdown carries no ERP or toll lines, no airport surcharge, no waiting-time fee and no promo discount, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing and produces no billing-integrity referral. The rider's profile point is accepted: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, below the POL-RD-08 thresholds of 4 and 1, so no extra corroboration burden attaches to this rider. No exculpatory clause was shown to answer the excess: no traffic advisory covers this trip (EV-ADVIS-04003-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run) and the chat log contains no rider instruction naming a place or road, so POL-RD-04's corroboration test cannot be run.\n\nWhat would resolve this for the reviewer: the missing stretch of GPS track, or an independent record of it — a rider-side GPS export, an ERP gantry record placing the vehicle on a corridor the booked route does not use, or a driver statement about the route. With that, the excess can be established or refuted and the POL-RD-02 figure above can be issued. Procedurally, this is a provisional ruling, and either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
